cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Agentic AI Library in research, teaching, engineering, benchmarking, or publications, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "Agentic AI Library: 170 Multi-Agent AI Reference Architectures Across 15 Domains"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Keikha
    given-names: Mahsa
repository-code: "https://github.com/MahsaKeikha/agentic_ai_library"
url: "https://github.com/MahsaKeikha/agentic_ai_library"
abstract: "An engineering atlas of 170 agentic AI and multi-agent reference systems spanning executive operations, AI engineering, software, healthcare, neuroscience, robotics, science, education, legal and compliance, manufacturing, marketing, creative work, public-sector workflows, finance and risk, and personal productivity. The library emphasizes specialized agents, orchestration, deterministic tools, explicit state, evidence, evaluation, observability, fail-closed governance, and human authority over consequential actions."
keywords:
  - agentic AI
  - multi-agent systems
  - AI agents
  - LLM agents
  - agent orchestration
  - agentic workflows
  - AI engineering
  - AI safety
  - human-in-the-loop
  - multi-agent architecture
